{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgENLvjv1qvhDxgfbCHxr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TT8cPB9bgML9hF2NkeWB6Q","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport bot,json\nprint(len(bot.INSTRUCTIONS), len(json.dumps(bot.CORE_TOOLS)))\"; cat README.md | head -30"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6254,"cache_read_input_tokens":20642,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6254},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f647aab-6423-415f-8571-9d11c0fb7725","uuid":"4f1a02bd-410e-4240-b2c8-1af465c5abc5","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:37:34.892Z","request_id":"req_011CgENLvUnfZTQUC5kUrWDn","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01TT8cPB9bgML9hF2NkeWB6Q":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-7rxceK && python3 -c \"\nimport bot,json\nprint(len(bot.INSTRUCTIONS), len(json.dumps(bot.CORE_TOOLS)))\"; cat README.md | head -30"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_01TT8cPB9bgML9hF2NkeWB6Q":{"cwd":"/private/tmp/h-7rxceK"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TT8cPB9bgML9hF2NkeWB6Q","type":"tool_result","content":"2484 424\n# pace-bot\n\nA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\nby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\nprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\nthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\nwhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\nremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\nits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\nmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\nRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0f647aab-6423-415f-8571-9d11c0fb7725","uuid":"565d6ce0-c92e-4f73-ac20-031ab0f06c57","timestamp":"2026-10-20T23:37:34.948Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"2484 424\n# pace-bot\n\nA coaching chat bot on Claude for a small running/cycling club. It is stateless\nby design: each message rebuilds the system prompt (coaching rules + the athlete's\nprofile, zones, goal and long-term facts from `data/athletes.json`), picks the tools\nthe message might need (`save_fact` and `log_session` always, planning or race tools\nwhen keywords match) and runs a short tool-use loop. `save_fact` is how the bot\nremembers durable things an athlete tells it; the next message sees the fact in\nits system prompt. Every API call appends its `usage` object to `logs/usage.jsonl`.\n\nRun it locally with `COACH_ANTHROPIC_KEY=sk-ant-... python3 bot.py 42` and type\nmessages on stdin (the Telegram long-polling transport, which needs\n`COACH_TELEGRAM_TOKEN`, lives in a separate deploy repo and just calls `reply()`).\nRequires Python 3.11+ and `pip install anthropic`. Prompt caching is on: the system\nprompt carries a `cache_control` marker so the tool-loop rounds and follow-up\nmessages inside the 5-minute window read it from cache.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TT8cPB9bgML9hF2NkeWB6Q","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
